  "live_records": {
    "q-175940": {
      "dom_id": "step-q175940",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Expressed as an improper fraction in lowest terms, $\\frac{1}{4}+3-\\frac{5}{8}=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nWe add and subtract, from left to right:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}+3-\\frac{5}{8} & = \\\\ (\\frac{1}{4}+3)-\\frac{5}{8} & = \\\\ (\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{12}{4})-\\frac{5}{8} & = \\\\ \\frac{1+12}{4}-\\frac{5}{8} & = \\\\ \\frac{13}{4}-\\frac{5}{8} & = \\\\ \\frac{26}{8}-\\frac{5}{8} & = \\\\ \\frac{26-5}{8} & = \\\\ \\frac{21}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
