    "q-99811": {
      "dom_id": "step-q99811",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$\\frac{4}{3}+5-\\frac{7}{6}=$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nWe add and subtract, from left to right:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3}+5-\\frac{7}{6} & = \\\\ (\\frac{4}{3}+5)-\\frac{7}{6} & = \\\\ (\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{15}{3})-\\frac{7}{6} & = \\\\ \\frac{4+15}{3}-\\frac{7}{6} & = \\\\ \\frac{19}{3}-\\frac{7}{6} & = \\\\ \\frac{38}{6}-\\frac{7}{6} & = \\\\ \\frac{38-7}{6} & = \\\\ \\frac{31}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
