      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Expressed as an integer, $8÷(-\\frac{4}{5})-3=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, we divide:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8÷(-\\frac{4}{5})-3 & = \\\\ (8÷(-\\frac{4}{5}))-3 & = \\\\ (\\frac{8}{1}\\times (-\\frac{5}{4}))-3 & = \\\\ -\\frac{8\\times 5}{1\\times 4}-3 & = \\\\ -\\frac{40}{4}-3 & = \\\\ -10-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we subtract:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10-3 & =-13\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
